From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] cache: fix cache_metadata_format_t pointer type mismatch

dm_config_get_uint32() expects a 'uint32_t *' for its result
argument, but struct lv_segment's cache_metadata_format field is
declared as 'cache_metadata_format_t', an incompatible pointer
type when its address is taken in
lib/cache_segtype/cache.c:_cache_pool_text_import() and
_cache_text_import(). GCC only warns about this, but Clang treats
-Wincompatible-pointer-types as an error by default, which breaks
the build with clang-based toolchains.

cache_metadata_format only ever holds CACHE_METADATA_FORMAT_*
values, so declaring the field as uint32_t preserves the existing
semantics while matching dm_config_get_uint32()'s prototype. All
other uses of this field are by value, not by address, so this is
a safe, narrowly-scoped change.

Signed-off-by: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
---
 lib/metadata/metadata-exported.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/metadata/metadata-exported.h b/lib/metadata/metadata-exported.h
index 3eda7d343..0bcd9552d 100644
--- a/lib/metadata/metadata-exported.h
+++ b/lib/metadata/metadata-exported.h
@@ -534,7 +534,7 @@
 	struct id *metadata_id;			/* For cache, when NULL uses CVOL id */
 	struct id *data_id;			/* For cache, when NULL uses CVOL id */

-	cache_metadata_format_t cache_metadata_format;/* For cache_pool */
+	uint32_t cache_metadata_format;/* For cache_pool */
 	cache_mode_t cache_mode;		/* For cache_pool */
 	const char *policy_name;		/* For cache_pool */
 	struct dm_config_node *policy_settings;	/* For cache_pool */
